    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31226" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴρων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span>, ὁ, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dissembler, one who says less than
				he thinks</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				449
			</span></i>, etc.; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀληθευτικός</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1124b30
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Char.</u>
				1.1
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλαζών</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1108a23
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλώπηξ εἴ. τῇ φύσει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philem.
					89.6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ εἴ. ὡς ἐπὶ τὸ πλεῖστον ἀλαζόνος
					εἶδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Vit.</u>
					p.38J.
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ. ἐν τοῖς λόγοις</span>”
